# Angular / TypeScript Conventions

## Shared Constants & Utilities

- Never define local `DOC_TYPE_ICONS` maps. Always import `docTypeIcon()` from `@nuxeo/satori-platform/nuxeo-client`.
- Domain-specific API methods (e.g. `fetchThumbnail`) belong in their domain service (`DocumentDetailService`), not in `NuxeoApiBase`.
- Keep shared constants, models, and utilities in `libs/shared/` — never duplicate across feature libs or apps.

## Routing & Component Reuse

- When a component reads route params, subscribe to `ActivatedRoute.paramMap` — never use `.snapshot` if the component can be reused across navigations.
- Always reset component state (signals, flags, blob URLs) when route params change.

## Signals & State

- Reset boolean loaded/error flags on failure so the user can retry.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — loaded stays true, retry impossible
error: () => {
  this.loading.set(false);
}

// ✅ GOOD
error: () => {
  this.loading.set(false);
  this.loaded = false;  // allows retry
}
```

## Dependency Injection

- Remove unused `inject()` calls. Every injected service must be referenced.
- Prefer injecting the most specific service, not a base class, when only one method is needed.
